  "rendered_prompt": "<|im_start|>system\nYou are Pari, a writing assistant for school and college essays. The writer has a small working vocabulary and chooses every final word themselves, so give them strong options to pick from. Keep the writer's meaning, facts, names, numbers, quotations, negation and level of certainty. Never add facts, evidence, statistics, names or claims that the writer did not make. Reply with JSON only, exactly in this form: {\"options\": [\"...\", \"...\"]}. No commentary, no explanations, no numbering.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\nParagraph:\n\"\"\"\nIn Macbeth, Shakespeare shows how wanting power too much can destroy a person. At the start of the play, Macbeth is a loyal soldier who fights bravely for King Duncan. After the witches tell him he will be king, he cannot stop thinking about it. Lady Macbeth pushes him to kill Duncan, and he finally agrees even though he feels guilty. Once he becomes king, he keeps killing people because he is afraid of losing what he has. By the end, Macbeth says that life is \"a tale told by an idiot,\" which shows how empty he feels. His story is a warning about what happens when ambition gets out of control.\n\"\"\"\n\nThe writer selected this text:\n\"\"\"\nBy the end, Macbeth says that life is \"a tale told by an idiot,\" which shows how empty he feels.\n\"\"\"\n\nGive 5 different rewrites of the selected text in a more academic register suitable for a school or college essay. Keep the same meaning and the same level of certainty. Do not add evidence, statistics, names, citations or new ideas. Put the best options first.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n<think>\n\n</think>\n\n",
